    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **255 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` field on owner creation: `true` when more than 80 owners had already been created for the owner's business day at registration time, `false` otherwise.\n\nFollowing the codebase's OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (mirroring the existing `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount` / `RejectOwnerDailyLimit` \"daily accumulation\" rules), the changes are:\n\n1. **`AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning.java`** (new) \u2014 a create-flow step that counts owners already sharing this owner's adjusted `registrationDate` (excluding itself, since it isn't saved yet) and sets `bulkSignupWarning = count > 80`. Same accumulation path as the daily-limit rule, at a lower non-rejecting threshold.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step into the pipeline (after `assignNamesakeCount`, before `save`, under the same transaction governance), so it runs once `registrationDate` is set.\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient` `bulkSignupWarning` field with getter/setter. It's a create-time snapshot, deliberately **not** persisted.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `bulkSignupWarning` as a read-only boolean on the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped it with a null-safe expression so owners loaded from the DB (which never carry the transient snapshot) return `false` rather than `null`, matching the GET assertion.\n\n### Key design decision\nI made the field **derived/transient rather than a DB column**. A persisted column would have required editing the `owners` table in all four `schema.sql` files *and* breaking every positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES(...)` row across all four `data.sql` seed files. The transient approach keeps the flag as a create-time snapshot on the response while leaving persistence and seed data untouched.\n\nThe new acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold`) passes: a fresh create followed by `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns `bulkSignupWarning: false`.",
